# counter harness. One force call is one clean energy and gradient.
# Noise is added after the call. A repeated coordinate keeps that sample.
# The index uses the clean Hessian. Six rigid modes are removed.
# A curvature is negative only below -max(force_norm, 1e-8*||H||_F, 1e-6).
# Energy and Kabsch RMSD are not applied: the problem file has no per-start reference.
# Default profile. fun and jac are the harness kernel. A repeated coordinate returns the cached sample and does not add a call. The per-atom cap is 0.2. A larger trial is mapped back inside that ball before the potential runs. The map is the identity through 0.18 and smooth beyond it. The stop is the noise-aware force norm, and at positive sigma the clean-energy window. The index is the clean Hessian with the rigid-mode rule.
